# Design system layers

Authoritative idea: [`docs/ideas/design-system-hardening.md`](../../docs/ideas/design-system-hardening.md).
When adding or splitting UI, follow [`.cursor/skills/add-ui-component/SKILL.md`](../skills/add-ui-component/SKILL.md).
When auditing an existing type for compose/refactor opportunities, follow [`.cursor/skills/evaluate-ui-component/SKILL.md`](../skills/evaluate-ui-component/SKILL.md).

Three layers (Brad Frost: components / recipes / snowflakes). **Stop at the highest layer you need** — do not wrap for completeness.

| Layer | Where | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| **Design system** | `DesignSystem/` (`PV*`) | Content-agnostic; tokens + slots only. No catalog / store / feature meaning. |
| **Recipes** | Shared product home (e.g. `Components/Research/`) | Provenencia-specific, **≥2 call sites**. Thin map onto `PV*`. |
| **Snowflakes** | `Features/<Feature>/` (`private`) | One screen. Promote on second real consumer. |

Inside the kit: **primitive** (button, panel) vs **composite** (confirm, form dialog) — same layer, different size. Prefer one panel + slots over a new root dialog.

```swift
// ❌ BAD — new PV* for one screen, or domain types inside DesignSystem
struct PVDeleteSourceFieldDialog { … }  // catalog meaning in the kit

// ✅ GOOD — DS composite at the call site; snowflake only for unique body
.pvConfirmSheet(item: pendingDelete, copy: deleteCopy(for:), …) { field in
    PVConfirmKeyChip(label: …, value: field.key)
}
```

- Compose down; don’t clone sideways for a slight variant.
- No dimming/scrim on sheets — window owns chrome (see `PVConfirm` / DesignSystem README).
- Search existing `PV*` before inventing chrome under `Features/`.
